<code>assert !\old(this.contains(oldValue)) || \old(this.indexOf(oldValue)) != index;</code>

Explanation: The comment states that if the value at the removed index occurred only once, it should remain present after removal. This means that either the value did not exist in the list before the removal (in which case the assertion is trivially true because `contains(oldValue)` would be false), or if it existed, its index should not be the one that was just removed. The assertion checks these conditions using the `\old` keyword to refer to the state before the removal.
